---
BPMN Kit command line

Usage: bpmnkit <COMMAND>

Commands:
  profile     Show profiles (read-only; other profile commands run in the legacy CLI)
  lint        Lint a BPMN file
  layout      Lay out a BPMN file (prints the XML, or writes -o / --in-place)
  diff        Compare two BPMN files
  render      Render a BPMN file as SVG (or PNG with -o x.png)
  convert     Convert Camunda 7 models to Camunda 8 and report what needs manual work
  connector   Connector templates: generate from OpenAPI, bind to a BPMN element
  completion  Print a shell completion script
  plugin      Inspect plugins
  self        Manage this installation
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Other commands run a `bpmnkit-<name>` plugin from PATH or <plugins dir>/bin, or fall
back to the legacy Node CLI (disable with BPMNKIT_NO_LEGACY=1). `casen` is an alias.
